                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "For the strong base, all of the particles are M"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and OH"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "−"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and none are the base MOH. For the weak base, most of the particles are the weak base (B), while a few particles are BH"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and OH"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "−"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". The difference in the particles occurs because a strong base completely (or nearly completely) ionizes in solution, while a weak base only partially ionizes in solution."
